  biomeName: Tier 17 South Reserve
  minDepthMeters: 7175
  maxDepthMeters: 7700
  shortDescription: Reserved biome slot for Tier 17 / South. The 108-biome matrix
    expects a bespoke authored identity here; final lore and geology are pending
    expansion from the master vision.
  isPlaceholder: 1
  visitPurpose: Deep-pressure biome. Come here with purpose, stronger gear, and a
    plan to work around bowls, pools, and local hotspots.
  commonRewardHook: Even routine value here comes from Iron Composite and Electrolyte
    Salts.
  rareRewardHook: 'The reason to risk the trip is: Rare Earth Dust and Stabilizer
    Coil.'
  landmarkIdentity: Tier 17 South Reserve reads through bowls, pools, domes, and
    hotspot basins. Landmarks should feel scarce but memorable.
  safePocketIdentity: 'Safe pockets are short-lived and mostly procedural: a lee
    side, a bowl edge, a dead current seam.'
  riskSummary: 'Main failure mode: localized danger pockets and hostile basins, depth
    stress, and expensive hesitation. Creature pressure stays medium_to_high.'
  extractionFocus: 'Sparse node hits and salvage pockets hidden in weak-visibility
    terrain. Deep tier: expect basin pockets, salvage traps, and local hotspots,
    extract only what justifies the risk, and leave cleanly.'
  landmarkGuidance: Dominant landmark is rare mound, trench lip, or wreck rise. This
    slot should read through almost absent silhouette with one lonely anchor; use
    bowls and hotspot rims to remember loops.
